# AI Usage Report

## Tool Used

I used ChatGPT as an AI-assisted development and documentation tool.

## Tools Used and Use Cases

ChatGPT was used during different stages of the assignment:

- Planning the structure of the interactive portfolio.
- Suggesting improvements to the visual design and user experience.
- Helping organize the HTML, CSS, JavaScript, image, and documentation files.
- Suggesting JavaScript for the dark and light mode feature.
- Helping create the interactive project modal.
- Helping connect project posters and video links.
- Helping add contact-form validation and user feedback.
- Reviewing the project structure and documentation.
- Improving the wording of the portfolio introduction and project descriptions.

## Benefits

Using AI helped me generate ideas more efficiently and understand how different web technologies work together.

It helped me understand:

- How JavaScript can respond to button clicks.
- How localStorage can save a user's theme preference.
- How a modal window can display dynamic content.
- How form validation can give feedback to users.
- How CSS transitions and hover effects can improve the user experience.
- How to organize a web project into separate files.

## Challenges and Limitations

Some AI suggestions needed to be checked and adjusted before using them. For example, file names and image paths had to match the actual files in my project.

I also needed to test the website because code that looks correct may still contain problems such as:

- Incorrect image paths.
- Missing HTML elements.
- Incorrect file names.
- Links that do not open correctly.
- Styling problems on smaller screens.

## Learning Outcomes

Through this assignment, I learned how to:

- Build a more interactive website using JavaScript.
- Use DOM selection and event listeners.
- Create a project modal that updates dynamically.
- Save user preferences using localStorage.
- Validate form fields.
- Display success and error messages.
- Use responsive CSS for different screen sizes.
- Improve the visual identity of a portfolio website.
- Organize project assets and documentation.

## Responsible Use and Modifications

I did not submit AI-generated code without reviewing it. I changed the content, project names, descriptions, images, colors, layout, and links to match my own work and identity.

I also tested the website in the browser and checked the main interactions myself. AI was used as a support tool for learning, problem-solving, design ideas, and documentation.

The final project represents my own portfolio and creative work.